<h1>PdMount third-party licences</h1>
<p>PdMount itself is MIT-licensed (the file LICENSE). The release binary contains the Rust crates listed here,
generated by cargo-about from Cargo.lock (about.toml, about.hbs), and the native code in the next section.
The source of every Rust crate is on crates.io; the Proton Drive SDK fork is at
<a href="https://github.com/colsen665/proton-sdk-rs2">github.com/colsen665/proton-sdk-rs2</a>.
Mozilla Public License 2.0 code (the option-ext crate, unmodified) is available from its source at
<a href="https://crates.io/crates/option-ext">crates.io/crates/option-ext</a>.</p>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2 id="native">Native code compiled into the binary</h2>
<p>cargo-about does not see code that a build script compiles from vendored sources:</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Go runtime and standard library</b> (the Go toolchain, linked into libgopenpgp_sys.a for proton-crypto), BSD-3-Clause, text below.
 The Go modules vendored in the gopenpgp-sys crate (gopenpgp, go-crypto, circl, golang.org/x/crypto, golang.org/x/sys)
 are listed in the crate licences under gopenpgp-sys.</li>
<li><b>SQLCipher</b> (Zetetic LLC, from the libsqlite3-sys crate, feature bundled-sqlcipher-vendored-openssl), BSD-3-Clause style, text below.
 It contains SQLite, which is in the public domain.</li>
<li><b>OpenSSL 3.x</b> (from the openssl-src crate, built statically for SQLCipher), Apache License 2.0, the text under "Apache License 2.0" below.
 Copyright The OpenSSL Project Authors.</li>
<li><b>AWS-LC</b> (aws-lc-sys crate), its licences are listed under that crate.</li>
</ul>
